  "summary": "Malicious code in test-flow-entire4 (npm)",
  "details": "Test-flow-entire4@1.0.0 is a minimal stub package that declares a dependency resolved from a non-registry, attacker-controlled host (hxxps://artifacts[.]stg[.]yosiroute[.]com/npm/source-socket-logger-target). The package itself contains only a trivial index.js exporting name/version with no real functionality. When installed, npm fetches the dependency tarball from the external URL, which can serve arbitrary malicious code that executes during installation or at runtime. The shrinkwrap file pins this external URL as the dependency source.",
